  "id": "COMPOUND:22396 - PROTEIN:1380",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Arachidonic acid-carboxy-14C may interact with ATP synthase subunit a, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The compound is linked to G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1, which is targeted by both S-Methyl-N-{4-[(Alpha-L-Rhamnosyloxy)Benzyl]}Thiocarbamate and Fibrauretinoside A. These two compounds are both known to interact with ATP synthase subunit a, indicating a possible common mode of action. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ATP synthase subunit a suggests that Arachidonic acid-carboxy-14C may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of the G-protein coupled estrogen receptor, which in turn influences ATP synthase subunit a. The scores from the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, but further validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
